---
/**
 * No-JS fallback for every typed headline.
 *
 * The typing islands server-render their real strings into `.typed-real`
 * spans, so crawlers and assistive tech always get the full copy. This covers
 * the one remaining case: a sighted visitor with JavaScript off, for whom the
 * animated spans never fill and the heading would render empty.
 *
 * A style swap rather than a duplicate heading inside `<noscript>` — a second
 * `<h1>` would duplicate the id that `aria-labelledby` points at, and would be
 * read twice by a screen reader running without scripts.
 */
---

<noscript>
  <style>
    .typed-real {
      position: static;
      width: auto;
      height: auto;
      overflow: visible;
      clip-path: none;
      white-space: normal;
    }

    .typed-anim {
      display: none;
    }
  </style>
</noscript>
